# Template for local development (no secrets needed yet).
# Copy to mobile/.env (the Expo project root loads it at build/start time).
# Mobile (Expo) — the app reads this at build/start time.
# For a physical phone, replace localhost with your computer's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.23:8000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
# Backend host/port are NOT read from the environment in this milestone.
# Pass them explicitly as uvicorn CLI flags (see README), e.g.
# --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 for local-only verification.
# LiveKit audio spike (development-only): paste the LiveKit Cloud development
# token-server ID into mobile/.env, never commit it. No static token is used:
# short-lived tokens are minted on demand at Start and expire after ~15 min.
# The ID allows unrestricted development token requests, so keep it unset by
# default and never use it for pilot or production builds.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVEKIT_TOKEN_SERVER_ID=
